MIOpen (pinned tag rocm-6.4.4): use scalar loads in spatial BatchNorm
variant 1 when H*W is not a multiple of 4, and fix the backward
recomputed-stats remainder offset.

WHY
---
MIOpen's spatial BatchNorm training forward (BnFwdTrainingSpatial,
src/kernels/MIOpenBatchNormFwdTrainSpatial.cl) and backward
(BnBwdTrainingSpatialSingle, src/kernels/MIOpenBatchNormBwdSpatial.cl)
select MIO_BN_VARIANT=1 whenever H*W > 1024 and N*H*W < 32M (and for
512 < H*W <= 1024 when N >= 32). In NCHW layout, variant 1 steps a
linear index k across N*H*W by 4 elements per thread (k = lid << 2,
stride GRPRD = 4*MIO_BN_GRP0), decomposes nidx = k / MIO_BN_HW and
hwidx = k - nidx * MIO_BN_HW, and reads _FLOAT4 vectors from
nidx * MIO_BN_CHW + grpid * MIO_BN_HW + hwidx. Backward uses this
vectorized loop for dscale/dbias at every variant-1 shape, and for
recomputed mean/variance (MIO_BN_USESAVED == 0) when MIO_BN_HW >= 4096;
forward training uses it for mean/variance when MIO_BN_HW >= 4096.

When MIO_BN_HW is not divisible by 4, stepping k by 4 across the
batch-spatial product crosses the end of a channel plane:
- The last _FLOAT4 read of batch plane nidx starts at
  hwidx = MIO_BN_HW - (MIO_BN_HW % 4) and reads 4 - (MIO_BN_HW % 4)
  elements past the end of channel grpid into channel grpid + 1 of the
  same batch item (for C > 1).
- The next multiple of 4 lands in batch plane nidx + 1 at
  hwidx = (4 - ((nidx + 1) * MIO_BN_HW) % 4) % 4, skipping the first
  1 to 3 elements of that plane and misaligning every subsequent
  _FLOAT4 load in that plane.
- In the remainder block (MIO_BN_REM4), threads with
  remkey >= MIO_BN_NHW compute nidx >= MIO_BN_N; the only bounds check
  is index < MIO_BN_NCHW - 3, and at the final valid elements of the
  last batch plane a partial tail < 4 elements fails that check and is
  dropped entirely (which is why C = 1 with N = 1 or 2 also fails).

In addition, MIOpenBatchNormBwdSpatial.cl's MIO_BN_USESAVED == 0
remainder block computes remkey = lid + MIO_BN_LESS4 instead of
(lid << 2) + MIO_BN_LESS4 (guarded by if(lid < MIO_BN_REM4)), whereas
MIOpenBatchNormFwdTrainSpatial.cl and the dscale/dbias loop in the same
file use (lid << 2) + MIO_BN_LESS4. Whenever MIO_BN_USESAVED is 0,
MIO_BN_HW >= 4096, and MIO_BN_REM4 > 0, threads read overlapping
_FLOAT4 vectors shifted by 1 float instead of 4.

Measured on an RX 590 (fp32 vs float64 CPU reference, PyTorch
F.batch_norm with training=True):
- Backward, NCHW: 16 of 81 shapes (N in {1,2,4}, C in {1,16,64}, H=W in
  {8,16,31,32,33,48,64,65,100}) are wrong, every one at H=W=33
  (HW=1089) or H=W=65 (HW=4225); dscale and dbias relative errors are
  1.3e-2 to 1.4e-1. H=W of 8, 16, 31, 32, 48, 64, and 100 are clean.
  Standalone reproduction without PyTorch:
    MIOpenDriver bnorm -n 2 -c 64 -H 33 -W 33 -m 1 --forw 0 -b 1 -r 1 --layout NCHW -V 1
  gives dscale error 0.062 (vs 0.0024 at 32x32) and dbias error 1.2e-3
  (vs 5.5e-8 at 32x32), while the driver still prints "verification
  passed" because its built-in tolerance is loose.
- Forward training, NCHW: 2x16x65x65 (HW=4225 >= 4096) has output error
  4.0e-3 and running-stat error ~1e-4; 1x16x65x65 has 2.4e-3;
  2x3x129x129 has 7.3e-4; 2x64x33x33 (HW=1089 < 4096, already on the
  scalar path in forward) and all HW % 4 == 0 shapes are at ~1e-6.

This is a generic index-arithmetic bug in architecture-independent
OpenCL kernel source, not specific to gfx803, and is still present
verbatim on upstream release/rocm-rel-7.1.

WHAT
----
1. In both MIOpenBatchNormBwdSpatial.cl and
   MIOpenBatchNormFwdTrainSpatial.cl under MIO_BN_VARIANT == 1, gate the
   NCHW _FLOAT4 reduction paths on (MIO_BN_HW % 4 == 0). When
   MIO_BN_HW % 4 != 0, use the existing scalar per-element loops
   (stepping by MIO_BN_GRP0 up to MIO_BN_LESS with the MIO_BN_REM tail
   guarded by index < MIO_BN_NCHW) with the NCHW element index
   nidx * MIO_BN_CHW + chwid + hwidx. NHWC and MIO_BN_HW % 4 == 0
   compilations are unchanged.
2. In MIOpenBatchNormBwdSpatial.cl's MIO_BN_USESAVED == 0 vectorized
   remainder block, compute remkey = (lid << 2) + MIO_BN_LESS4 to match
   the 4-element stride of the _FLOAT4 load, as
   MIOpenBatchNormFwdTrainSpatial.cl already does.

REAL-HARDWARE VERIFICATION (RX 590, this image)
Backward: 0 of the same 81 shapes wrong. Forward training at 1x16x65x65,
2x16x65x65, 4x16x65x65 and 2x3x129x129: output error 6e-7 to 1.2e-6,
running statistics below 1e-7. The MIOpenDriver command above gives
dscale 0.0028 and dbias 6.1e-8 at 33x33, the same as at 32x32. A
GPU-against-CPU sweep of BatchNorm forward and backward (MIOpen and
PyTorch's native kernel, NCHW and NHWC, fp32 and fp16, six shapes) has
no failures. Forward plus backward time is unchanged at 65x65 and
129x129 (0.471 against 0.474 ms, 1.875 against 1.891 ms). The image's
conv, SD1.5 UNet, rocPRIM and top-k checks and a 20-step LoRA training
run give the same results as before the patch.

diff --git a/src/kernels/MIOpenBatchNormBwdSpatial.cl b/src/kernels/MIOpenBatchNormBwdSpatial.cl
index a018d35..4731fec 100644
--- a/src/kernels/MIOpenBatchNormBwdSpatial.cl
+++ b/src/kernels/MIOpenBatchNormBwdSpatial.cl
@@ -311,7 +311,9 @@ MIOpenBatchNormBwdSpatial(const __global _FLOAT* __restrict x_in,
 #if(MIO_BN_USESAVED == 0)
     //==== CALC MEAN and VARIANCE ONCE AGAIN =======================
     _FLOAT_PREC variance = (_FLOAT_PREC)0.;
-#if !MIO_LAYOUT_NHWC && MIO_BN_HW >= 4096
+    // GFX803_BN_VARIANT1_UNALIGNED_HW: _FLOAT4 loads across NHW require each
+    // channel plane MIO_BN_HW to be a multiple of 4 so loads do not straddle planes.
+#if !MIO_LAYOUT_NHWC && MIO_BN_HW >= 4096 && (MIO_BN_HW % 4 == 0)
     _FLOAT4 read4;
 #if(MIO_BN_N > MIO_BN_LOOP_UNROLL_MAXN)
     __attribute__((opencl_unroll_hint(4))) for(unsigned int k = lid << 2; k < MIO_BN_LESS4;
@@ -336,24 +338,21 @@ MIOpenBatchNormBwdSpatial(const __global _FLOAT* __restrict x_in,
     }
 
 #if(MIO_BN_REM4)
-    if(lid < MIO_BN_REM4)
+    unsigned int remkey = (lid << 2) + MIO_BN_LESS4;
+    nidx                = remkey / MIO_BN_HW;
+    hwidx               = remkey - (nidx * MIO_BN_HW);
+    index               = nidx * MIO_BN_CHW + chwid + hwidx;
+    if(index < (MIO_BN_NCHW - 3))
     {
-        unsigned int remkey = lid + MIO_BN_LESS4;
-        nidx                = remkey / MIO_BN_HW;
-        hwidx               = remkey - (nidx * MIO_BN_HW);
-        index               = nidx * MIO_BN_CHW + chwid + hwidx;
-        if(index < (MIO_BN_NCHW - 3))
-        {
-            read4 = *((const global _FLOAT4*)(x_in + index));
-            mean += FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.x);
-            mean += FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.y);
-            mean += FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.z);
-            mean += FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.w);
-            variance = mad(FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.x), FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.x), variance);
-            variance = mad(FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.y), FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.y), variance);
-            variance = mad(FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.z), FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.z), variance);
-            variance = mad(FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.w), FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.w), variance);
-        }
+        read4 = *((const global _FLOAT4*)(x_in + index));
+        mean += FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.x);
+        mean += FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.y);
+        mean += FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.z);
+        mean += FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.w);
+        variance = mad(FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.x), FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.x), variance);
+        variance = mad(FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.y), FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.y), variance);
+        variance = mad(FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.z), FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.z), variance);
+        variance = mad(FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.w), FLOAT2FLOATPREC(read4.w), variance);
     }
 #endif
 #else
@@ -420,6 +419,42 @@ MIOpenBatchNormBwdSpatial(const __global _FLOAT* __restrict x_in,
 
 #endif
 
+#if !MIO_LAYOUT_NHWC && (MIO_BN_HW % 4 != 0)
+    _FLOAT dyRead;
+    _FLOAT xread;
+    _FLOAT_PREC xhat_tmp;
+#if(MIO_BN_N > MIO_BN_LOOP_UNROLL_MAXN)
+    __attribute__((opencl_unroll_hint(4))) for(unsigned int k = lid; k < MIO_BN_LESS;
+                                               k += MIO_BN_GRP0)
+#else
+    __attribute__((opencl_unroll_hint(2))) for(unsigned int k = lid; k < MIO_BN_LESS;
+                                               k += MIO_BN_GRP0)
+#endif
+    {
+        nidx     = k / MIO_BN_HW;
+        hwidx    = k - (nidx * MIO_BN_HW);
+        index    = nidx * MIO_BN_CHW + chwid + hwidx;
+        xread    = *((const global _FLOAT*)(x_in + index));
+        dyRead   = *((const global _FLOAT*)(dy_in + index));
+        xhat_tmp = (FLOAT2FLOATPREC(xread) - mean) * invVariance;
+        db += FLOAT2FLOATPREC(dyRead);
+        ds = mad(xhat_tmp, FLOAT2FLOATPREC(dyRead), ds);
+    }
+#if(MIO_BN_REM)
+    unsigned int remkey = lid + MIO_BN_LESS;
+    nidx                = remkey / MIO_BN_HW;
+    hwidx               = remkey - (nidx * MIO_BN_HW);
+    index               = nidx * MIO_BN_CHW + chwid + hwidx;
+    if(index < MIO_BN_NCHW)
+    {
+        xread    = *((const global _FLOAT*)(x_in + index));
+        dyRead   = *((const global _FLOAT*)(dy_in + index));
+        xhat_tmp = (FLOAT2FLOATPREC(xread) - mean) * invVariance;
+        db += FLOAT2FLOATPREC(dyRead);
+        ds = mad(xhat_tmp, FLOAT2FLOATPREC(dyRead), ds);
+    }
+#endif
+#else
 #if MIO_LAYOUT_NHWC
     _FLOAT dyRead;
     _FLOAT xread;
@@ -502,6 +537,7 @@ MIOpenBatchNormBwdSpatial(const __global _FLOAT* __restrict x_in,
 #endif
     }
 
+#endif
 #endif
     barrier(CLK_GLOBAL_MEM_FENCE);
 
